WEBVTT

00:00.251 --> 00:02.133
[SPEAKER_00]: First session with Paul Rivero.

00:02.214 --> 00:03.515
[SPEAKER_01]: This is Julian's character.

00:05.217 --> 00:08.341
[SPEAKER_01]: And kind of a background information on this.

00:08.841 --> 00:12.586
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll let you know that I record most of the session basically to take notes.

00:12.606 --> 00:14.088
[SPEAKER_00]: That's awesome.

00:14.548 --> 00:17.872
[SPEAKER_00]: And I have this program where I put it through a translator.

00:18.862 --> 00:27.284
[SPEAKER_00]: That puts it into text, and then I summarize it using the AI, and I give it to my players to be able to read, to remember.

00:27.504 --> 00:28.744
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, so you do this for everyone?

00:28.884 --> 00:30.285
[SPEAKER_00]: What happened, yeah, everybody.

00:30.305 --> 00:32.065
[SPEAKER_00]: I've got programs that take care of all this stuff.

00:32.245 --> 00:34.546
[SPEAKER_00]: Wow, that's a whole new level.

00:34.786 --> 00:37.986
[SPEAKER_00]: So you'll get an email.

00:38.187 --> 00:43.568
[SPEAKER_00]: Probably what I'll do is create a Google Docs that you can go and click on and just see the history of everything that's happened for you.

00:43.668 --> 00:44.028
[SPEAKER_00]: Awesome.

00:44.428 --> 00:45.708
[SPEAKER_00]: So you don't have to take notes.

00:45.808 --> 00:48.029
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, if you want to take notes, you can take notes as well.

00:49.269 --> 01:01.313
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, what I don't do, and this is really a huge part of the game, is I do not allow characters to listen to sessions where they're talking to other characters.

01:01.814 --> 01:04.855
[SPEAKER_01]: Like one-on-ones and... Well, conversations.

01:04.875 --> 01:08.036
[SPEAKER_01]: Or conversations with one character specific, is what you're saying.

01:08.316 --> 01:12.417
[SPEAKER_00]: And the reason I do that is I like to have...

01:15.252 --> 01:25.268
[SPEAKER_00]: I like to have the interactions of people that are disagreeing about things and the way they view it and see it without there being a definitive God, you know, message, right?

01:25.288 --> 01:27.431
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, yeah, it's like you know but you don't know.

01:27.772 --> 01:29.574
[SPEAKER_00]: If there's something you do by yourself,

01:31.061 --> 01:40.746
[SPEAKER_00]: Or if there's a conversation with an NPC that's very important, I will sometimes let people go through and look at the transcript of that so they can remember that.

01:41.106 --> 01:46.049
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's basically because, you know, NPCs are NPCs.

01:46.089 --> 01:57.555
[SPEAKER_00]: However, other player characters, if you have a conflict or if there's a misunderstanding or whatever, because oftentimes, and I'm not saying everybody does this, but oftentimes there will be disagreements.

01:58.486 --> 02:00.088
[SPEAKER_00]: And somebody will act unreasonable.

02:17.780 --> 02:21.483
[SPEAKER_00]: It's important to be mindful when you're playing with other player characters in this situation.

02:21.503 --> 02:27.888
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, I mean, usually you do not get in conflict with other player characters in a way where it's like you're fighting them.

02:27.948 --> 02:28.228
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

02:28.609 --> 02:29.690
[SPEAKER_00]: Even though it does happen.

02:30.170 --> 02:30.730
[SPEAKER_01]: It has happened.

02:30.750 --> 02:35.674
[SPEAKER_01]: I think it's only ever happened to me once in like all seven D&D campaigns I've ever played.

02:35.775 --> 02:36.035
[SPEAKER_00]: Right.

02:36.195 --> 02:39.918
[SPEAKER_00]: But in this game, there are a lot of disagreements between friends.

02:40.478 --> 02:40.678
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

02:40.899 --> 02:44.982
[SPEAKER_00]: And a lot of it occurs because of misunderstandings and miscommunications that occur.

02:49.689 --> 02:52.872
[SPEAKER_00]: I just misremembered, which is part of the game.

02:52.972 --> 02:57.596
[SPEAKER_00]: So that is something I want to tell you up front.

02:58.036 --> 03:03.661
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, so background of your character, right?

03:05.163 --> 03:11.449
[SPEAKER_00]: Alright, so first off, you are

03:13.262 --> 03:18.706
